        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Newer hardware typically commands higher prices. The exception is Wavlink\u2019s 12-in-1 Thunderbolt 5 dock, which offers a fantastic opportunity to upgrade your home office for an excellent price of $195, or 35 percent off for Prime Day.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>I\u2019ve <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/393714/best-thunderbolt-docks-for-a-laptop-pc.html\">personally reviewed dozens of Thunderbolt docks for PCWorld</a> \u2014 and for the ones I haven\u2019t, my colleagues at Macworld pick up the slack. Amazon\u2019s selling the <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/WAVLINK-Certified-Thunderbolt-Transfer-Ethernet/dp/B0FRG475YC?tag=pcworld02-20&#038;asc_refurl=https://www.pcworld.com\">Wavlink 12-in-1 Thunderbolt 5 dock for $195</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.macworld.com/article/3009184/wavlink-thunderbolt-5-dock-review.html\">Macworld awarded this dock an Editor\u2019s Choice award</a>. Yes please.</p>",
