        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>On June 24th\u2014that\u2019s tomorrow, as of this writing\u2014Windows users will run into an important deadline: new Secure Boot certificates must be installed on all systems that use Secure Boot, the security feature that protects against various threats at startup. The first warning about updated certificates was issued <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/3035032/are-you-still-on-windows-10-you-should-install-the-latest-update.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">back in January</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If your system doesn\u2019t get new Secure Boot certificates, you could <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/3148507/your-pcs-trust-in-windows-has-an-expiration-date.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">run into serious problems</a>. Without these certificates, there\u2019s no guarantee that Secure Boot will continue to work properly. In the worst case scena",
